# NOT FOR master.
#
# The vocabulary of the `openbaarheid van bestuur` demonstration process,
# on the branch `poc-startup-gate` and nowhere else.
#
# Unlike the `oe:` terms in `poc-ontology-terms.ttl`, this namespace has
# no document on master at all. That is a different kind of gap and the
# engine says so differently: a term that is missing can be defined in
# the file its namespace already has, but a namespace nobody claims is a
# missing *file* — there is nowhere to put the definition. This file is
# that nowhere, for as long as the process is a proof of concept.
#
# Every term is `unstable`. Nothing here carries master's append-only
# promise.

@prefix ovb:   <https://id.erfgoed.net/vocab/openbaarheidvanbestuur#>.
@prefix dct:   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>.
@prefix owl:   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>.
@prefix prov:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#>.
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>.
@prefix vann:  <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/>.
@prefix vs:    <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#>.
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.

### 1. Basic info about this vocabulary

<https://id.erfgoed.net/vocab/openbaarheidvanbestuur> a owl:Ontology;
    rdfs:label "Openbaarheid van bestuur (proof of concept)"@nl-BE;
    dct:created "2026-10-29"^^xsd:date;
    dct:modified "2026-10-29"^^xsd:date;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "ovb";
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://id.erfgoed.net/vocab/openbaarheidvanbestuur#";
    vs:term_status "unstable";
    dct:description """The process vocabulary of the openbaarheid-van-bestuur
    demonstration process carried by the dossier platform. A proof of concept:
    the terms are named by a running workflow definition, not by a published
    standard, and they are defined here so that the platform's startup gate can
    resolve them."""@en.

